      "id": "idea",
      "narration": "Sage explains the first law. Every habit starts with a cue, a trigger your brain notices. A snack left on the counter. A phone glowing on the desk. Then temptation strolls in, right on schedule, offering the easy bad habit. The fix is simple to say. Make the good cues loud and impossible to miss, and make the bad cues quietly disappear.",
